<form class="{{cssClass}}" autocomplete="off">
    <div class="form-group">
        <h2>{{actor.name}}</h2>
    </div>

    <fieldset>
        <legend>Configuration</legend>
        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label><i class="fa-regular fa-brain-circuit"></i> AI Enabled</label>
            <input type="checkbox" name="enabled" {{checked config.enabled}}>
        </div>
        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label><i class="fa-regular fa-gear"></i> AI Model</label>
            <select name="model">
                {{#select config.model}}
                <option value="default">World Default</option>
                <option value="v1">Fast - Faster and Cheaper - Costs 1 message per chat message. Great for your general run-of-the mill mooks and mobs.</option>
                <option value="hybrid">Hybrid - The default model. Costs 1 message per chat message. Not as fast as the Fast model, but more capable. Great for your Shopkeeps, Tavern Keepers, etc.</option>
                <option value="v2">Enhanced - More Capable and Nuanced, but costs 10 messages per chat message. Great for your setpiece bosses and NPCS your party will interact with often.</option>
                {{/select}}
            </select>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>Journal Page <i class="inpc-journal-page-link fas fa-file-lines" data-uuid="{{journalPageUUID}}"></i></label>
            {{#if canSwap}}
                {{#unless journalPageUUID}}
                    <p class="notes">No page selected yet. Pick one from the dropdown below, or scaffold one in a click:</p>
                    <button type="button" class="inpc-create-page"><i class="fas fa-wand-magic-sparkles"></i> Create new page from this actor</button>
                    <p class="notes" style="margin-top:0.4em">Other options: <b>Browse Free NPCs</b> on the Journal sidebar to import a pre-made character, or manually create a new Journal entry → page → switch the page sheet to <i>Intelligent NPC Configuration</i>.</p>
                {{else}}
                    <p class="notes">Pick an available Intelligent NPC journal page to swap personality. The current selection shows below.</p>
                {{/unless}}
            {{else}}
                <p class="notes">This NPC has runtime customizations (memory, goals, objectives, or message history). <b>Reset</b> wipes all of those and restores the journal page's starting values — required before you can swap to a different page.</p>
                <button class="reset-inpc"><i class="fas fa-undo"></i> Reset</button>
            {{/if}}
            <select name="journalPage" {{#unless canSwap}}disabled="disabled"{{/unless}}>
                {{#select config.journalPage}}
                <option value="none">None</option>
                {{#each journalPages.optgroups}}
                    <optgroup label="{{label}}">
                        {{#each options}}
                            <option value="{{value}}">{{label}}</option>
                        {{/each}}
                    </optgroup>
                {{/each}}
                {{/select}}
            </select>
        </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
        <legend>Public</legend>
        <p class="notes">These fields override any journal selected, and will be read by other Intelligent NPCs, so don't include any info that others shouldn't generally know</p>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>What Everyone Knows</label>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="4" name="whatEveryoneKnows" placeholder="{{actor.name}} is a generic person who is well known for existing." maxlength="500">{{config.whatEveryoneKnows}}</textarea>
            <p class="notes">A quick summary of what others generally know about this person. Write in third person. Max length: 500 characters</p>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>Appearance</label>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="3" name="appearance" placeholder="{{actor.name}} wears standard street wear." maxlength="500">{{config.appearance}}</textarea>
            <p class="notes">What this character looks like to others. Write in third person. Overrides the Journal details if set. Max length: 500 characters</p>
        </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
        <legend>Advanced</legend>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>Memory</label>
            <p class="notes">The NPC's running long-term memory. <b>Overrides the journal page</b> — leave empty to inherit the page's starting memory. Generally best to let the NPC manage its own memory; the secondary CoreMemory loop will compact this automatically over long conversations.</p>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="5" name="memory" placeholder="Memory">{{config.memory}}</textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>Goals</label>
            <p class="notes">The NPC's current priorities. <b>Overrides the journal page</b> — leave empty to inherit. The NPC may rewrite this when its goals shift; you can also edit it directly.</p>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="3" name="goals" placeholder="Goals">{{config.goals}}</textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>Objectives</label>
            <p class="notes">Active to-do list — markdown checklist, e.g. <code>- [ ] Find the keg thief</code> or <code>- [x] Pour Cody his ale</code>. <b>Overrides the journal page</b> — leave empty to inherit. The NPC drives toward open items, marks them complete as they finish, and may add new items when taking on a task. Works best on the Quality tier.</p>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="4" name="objectives" placeholder="- [ ] First objective&#10;- [ ] Second objective">{{config.objectives}}</textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group-stacked">
            <label>Message History</label>
            <p class="notes">The raw transcript the NPC remembers from its conversations. You usually don't need to read it — click <b>Clear History</b> to start the NPC fresh.</p>
            <button class="clear-history"><i class="fas fa-trash"></i> Clear History</button>
            <textarea class="form-control" rows="10" readonly placeholder="Message History">{{messageHistory}}</textarea>
        </div>
    </fieldset>
</form>
